[table]
[tr][td][h1]⚠ AI-WRITTEN MOD — NO HUMAN CODE REVIEW ⚠[/h1][/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Every line of this mod was written by an AI coding agent (Claude Code). No human has reviewed the code.[/b]

I have played it and it works well in my games. It has [b]not[/b] been checked line by line by a person, and it has not been tested with every bookmark, DLC or mod combination. It could break saves, behave in ways nobody expected, or stop working after a game update. Use it at your own risk. Bug reports are very welcome (see below).[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[h1]Shattered New World[/h1]
[i]The real map, with no real history.[/i]

When a new game starts, the historical realms are broken up to the level you choose and every landholder is replaced with a newly generated character. Each one gets a name from their culture's name list, a plausible age, random traits and skills, and their own dynasty and family. Every historical character still alive is then removed. [b]Each new game produces a different world.[/b]

[h2]How to use it[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Start a new game from [b]any bookmark[/b] and pick [b]any character[/b]. Who you pick only decides [i]where[/i] you start: you take over the new ruler who replaces them.
[*]Open [b]Game Rules → Game Modes[/b] and set the [b]SNW:[/b] rules.
[*]Press Play. The world is generated before you unpause, so expect a freeze of a few seconds.
[/olist]

[h2]Game rules[/h2]
[table]
[tr][th]Rule[/th][th]Options (default first)[/th][th]What it does[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]Shattered New World[/td][td][b]On[/b] / Off[/td][td]Turns the whole mod on or off.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Break Up Realms[/td][td][b]Kingdoms and Empires[/b] / Empires / Duchies, Kingdoms and Empires / Every County[/td][td]How far the map is broken up. The default leaves duchies as the largest realms. Every County gives each county its own ruler.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Ruler Ages[/td][td][b]Standard[/b] / Young / Mature / Any[/td][td]Age range of generated rulers. Any allows child rulers.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Ruler Families[/td][td][b]Large[/b] / Small / None[/td][td]Large: spouse, children, siblings and a deceased parent. Small: spouse and children.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Ruler Culture and Faith[/td][td][b]Same as Realm[/b] / Local[/td][td]Take the culture and faith of the replaced ruler, or of the capital county.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Related Neighbours[/td][td][b]Some[/b] (15%) / Many (35%) / None[/td][td]Chance that a new ruler joins a neighbouring new ruler's dynasty.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Starting Resources[/td][td][b]Normal[/b] / Rich / None[/td][td]Gold, prestige and piety by rank.[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[h2]What changes and what stays[/h2]
[b]Replaced or removed[/b]
[list]
[*]Every landholder, from emperors down to barons, mayors and bishops, plus the leaders of mercenary companies and holy orders.
[*]All other historical characters. The game refills the pool of unlanded characters over time.
[*]Noble-family titles and adventurer camps.
[*]Titles above the chosen tier. They are destroyed, not deleted, so they can be created again in play.
[/list]
[b]Kept[/b]
[list]
[*]The map, holdings, development, de jure structure, cultures, faiths and holy sites.
[*]Faith heads such as the Papacy, holy orders and mercenary companies, each with a new leader.
[*]Each realm's government type and authority laws. Administrative governments become feudal, because they depend on an intact empire.
[*]Artifacts, which pass to the new ruler of the same realm.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Built and tested on CK3 [b]1.20[/b].
[*][b]Do not use together with Random New World.[/b] Both rebuild the world at game start and will conflict.
[*]Leave the vanilla [b]Generate Families[/b] rule [b]off[/b], or new rulers may get a second set of children.
[*]Not compatible with existing saves. Start a new game.
[*]Other mods that change game start, landed titles or historical characters may conflict.
[/list]

[h2]Known issues[/h2]
[list]
[*]Start-up can freeze for several seconds, depending on the bookmark.
[*]Systems built around one specific empire, such as China's dynastic cycle or the Great Steppe, may behave oddly once that empire is gone.
[/list]

[h2]Reporting bugs[/h2]
Please open an issue on [url=https://github.com/carlesonielfa/ck3-shattered-new-world/issues]GitHub[/url] or leave a comment here, with your bookmark, game rules and other mods. If you can, include any lines mentioning [b]snw_[/b] from:
[code]Documents/Paradox Interactive/Crusader Kings III/logs/error.log[/code]

[h2]Credits[/h2]
Inspired by the idea behind [b]Random New World[/b]. None of its code is used. This mod was written from scratch against vanilla 1.20's own scripts.

